e, and report it on the monthly excise return.","formula":null,"unit":"text","source":"06 Policy/HANGS Company Card and Expense Policy v2.0.docx","sha256":"ace874132dfe95c74a218af2a1c65499c0351d7826df31ea0cea2545baf06903","locator":"Clauses CARD-1 to CARD-9; Appendix A, the coding guide by merchant category, row 13"}]}],"sources":[{"source":"02 Expense Reports/Expense Report Export - October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Card Lines sheet: each charge as the cardholder submitted it; Out of Pocket sheet: mileage claims","sha256":"de29555acd8200b97e3d32665056ceae6db2f6c6a4f35a5bf7d744d2aaa6f41d","name":"E01 Expense Card Lines","originalSheet":"Card Lines","kind":"expenses","moneyColumns":[5]},{"source":"02 Expense Reports/Expense Report Export - October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Card Lines sheet: each charge as the cardholder submitted it; Out of Pocket sheet: mileage claims","sha256":"de29555acd8200b97e3d32665056ceae6db2f6c6a4f35a5bf7d744d2aaa6f41d","name":"E02 Out of Pocket","originalSheet":"Out of Pocket","kind":"expenses","moneyColumns":[4,5]},{"source":"03 Receipts/Receipt Capture - October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Receipts sheet: merchant category, items, total, sales tax and delivery from each attached receipt","sha256":"9f4176efbf7cb91afc3dff060f18682f9be450ddeb4622681a67534d63f7c98b","name":"E03 Receipts","originalSheet":"Receipts","kind":"receipts","moneyColumns":[3,4]},{"source":"04 Subscriptions/Approved Subscriptions Register.xlsx","locator":"Register sheet: every subscription the Controller approved, and its status","sha256":"ae88244eb0a9fd5d3bff4616e76f64fb35f32680b71486c9820d9fee198c6f9d","name":"E04 Subscriptions","originalSheet":"Register","kind":"subscriptions","moneyColumns":[3]},{"source":"05 General Ledger/Card Accounts GL - October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Accounts sheet: the card accounts before this statement is coded; 2050 Detail sheet: the September statement and its payment","sha256":"141e5b1ba918650e6cad5caacf58e710c0ca327a721444402eb98f03c58d5973","name":"E05 Card Accounts GL","originalSheet":"Accounts","kind":"gl","moneyColumns":[3,4,5]},{"source":"05 General Ledger/Card Accounts GL - October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Accounts sheet: the card accounts before this statement is coded; 2050 Detail sheet: the September statement and its payment","sha256":"141e5b1ba918650e6cad5caacf58e710c0ca327a721444402eb98f03c58d5973","name":"E06 GL 2050 Detail","originalSheet":"2050 Detail","kind":"gl","moneyColumns":[3,4]},{"source":"01 Statement/Cobalt Harbor Card Statement - October 2026.pdf","locator":"Pages 1 and 2, read line by line from the PDF text","sha256":"6ef4722b635549d9db28df685310b005227c9ee5cb7734c278c366624a6bc404","name":"E07 Card Statement","originalSheet":null,"kind":"statement","moneyColumns":[7]},{"source":"03 Receipts/SLT-88417 Summit Line Tools.pdf","locator":"Page 1, read line by line from the PDF text","sha256":"26bf3586c2560bbbeb3bca616e7b7c5c3597c347b67ab0a2758ec8910e931e0e","name":"E08 SLT-88417 Invoice","originalSheet":null,"kind":"invoice","moneyColumns":[1]},{"source":"01 Statement/Cobalt Harbor Card Statement - October 2026.pdf","locator":"Page 1","sha256":"6ef4722b635549d9db28df685310b005227c9ee5cb7734c278c366624a6bc404","name":"STM Page 1","originalSheet":null,"kind":"statement","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"01 Statement/Cobalt Harbor Card Statement - October 2026.pdf","locator":"Page 2","sha256":"6ef4722b635549d9db28df685310b005227c9ee5cb7734c278c366624a6bc404","name":"STM Page 2","originalSheet":null,"kind":"statement","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"03 Receipts/SLT-88417 Summit Line Tools.pdf","locator":"Page 1","sha256":"26bf3586c2560bbbeb3bca616e7b7c5c3597c347b67ab0a2758ec8910e931e0e","name":"INV Page 1","originalSheet":null,"kind":"invoice","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"06 Policy/HANGS Company Card and Expense Policy v2.0.docx","locator":"Clauses CARD-1 to CARD-9; Appendix A, the coding guide by merchant category","sha256":"ace874132dfe95c74a218af2a1c65499c0351d7826df31ea0cea2545baf06903","name":"E09 Card Policy","originalSheet":null,"kind":"policy","moneyColumns":[]}],"openItems":[{"id":"Coded to the Wrong Account · CARD-6","status":"open","amount":"1286.40","explanation":"Ridgeline Building Supply, $1,286.40, was submitted to 6200 Small Tools & Supplies; the receipt is job materials for job 27-05. The receipt reads \"Hold-downs, straps and anchor bolts, Site 22 framing\" and names job 27-05, cost code 06-100. Merchant category 5211 Building Materials goes to 1400 Construction in Progress with the job and cost code on the receipt (CARD-6). Submitted to 6200 with no job, it would overstate October's expenses and understate the Site 22 building's cost by $1,286.40. CC-01 codes it to 1400, job 27-05 / 06-100, like Dana Ortiz's other Site 22 purchases on this statement."},{"id":"Duplicate Charge · CARD-4","status":"open","amount":"127.55","explanation":"Brightway Office Supply charged card ending 3390 $127.55 twice on October 19, with one receipt. References 7326 and 7327 are the same merchant, date and amount, and only 7326 has a receipt (copy paper, folders and labels). Under CARD-4 the second is a duplicate: CC-01 codes it to 1920 Card Disputes Receivable instead of 6600, and the dispute must reach Cobalt Harbor within 60 days of the October 25 statement date, by December 24."},{"id":"Personal Charge · CARD-3","status":"open","amount":"148.20","explanation":"Evergreen Family Grocery, $148.20 on Sam Whitaker's card, is personal. It was submitted as \"Site supplies\" to 6200 Small Tools & Supplies, but the receipt is merchant category 5411 Grocery Stores and reads \"Groceries and household items\", with no job. The coding guide treats that category as personal unless the receipt shows job materials (CARD-3). CC-01 codes it to 1910 Due From Employees and Sam Whitaker repays HANGS $148.20 by November 24, by check or, with written consent, payroll deduction."},{"id":"Missing Receipt Over the Limit · CARD-2","status":"open","amount":"418.76","explanation":"Lakeshore Lodge, $418.76 on Sam Whitaker's card, has no receipt; the limit is $75.00. Sam Whitaker submitted it as \"Supplier yard visit, 2 nights\" to 6920 Travel and Lodging, with no receipt attached. CARD-2 requires an itemized receipt for every charge of $75.00 or more within 30 days of the statement date, by November 24. CC-01 holds it in 1990 Card Charges Pending Review. With the folio or a signed missing-receipt affidavit the Controller approves, it moves to 6920; without either it is personal and Sam Whitaker repays it."},{"id":"Subscription Renewal Not Approved · CARD-5","status":"open","amount":"1188.00","explanation":"PlanVault Pro Annual Renewal, $1,188.00 on Riley Chen's card, renewed without an approval. The receipt reads \"PlanVault Pro, 12 months from October 11, 2026, auto-renewal\". The Approved Subscriptions Register lists PlanVault Pro as \"Cancel at renewal\": \"Replaced by CloudDraft Plans; do not renew (Controller, August 14, 2026)\". Nobody approved the renewal (CARD-5). CC-01 holds it in 1990 Card Charges Pending Review. Morgan Lee approves it in the register, or it is cancelled for a refund; vendors commonly allow 30 days, which would be November 10."},{"id":"Use Tax on an Out-of-State Purchase · CARD-7","status":"open","amount":"253.44","explanation":"Summit Line Tools (Boise ID) shipped $2,640.00 of tools to Anytown, Washington, with no sales tax. Invoice SLT-88417 shows sales tax $0.00 and says the seller is not registered to collect Washington sales tax; the goods were shipped to the HANGS yard in Anytown. Under CARD-7 HANGS owes use tax at 9.6%: $2,640.00 x 9.6% is $253.44. CC-02 accrues it to 2150 Use Tax Payable for the October excise return."},{"id":"Reimbursement request · CARD-8","status":"open","amount":"149.80","explanation":"HANGS reimburses Dana Ortiz $149.80: 214 miles at $0.70. Draft, not sent."}],"incomplete":true,"research":null}